# --concurrent false: the lint-staged globs overlap by design and both
# entries write src TS files. lint-staged defaults to running every glob's
# commands at once, which races them on one file and commits whichever
# write landed last. Serial execution runs them in the order package.json
# declares, which is the order they need:
#
#   1. eslint --fix   (src TS — may rewrap code)
#   2. prettier       (everything — must be last so it formats 1's output)
#
# CI catches a bad interleaving, but as a confusing red build rather than a
# clean commit.
npx lint-staged --concurrent false
